{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01VKoDit7b1kmPtUtAoxVKwc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Anchor is a personal productivity + R&D mission-control system. Grounded summary of what it IS:\n\n- **Purpose: a single-folder productivity system for one user (J.C. Liechty).** Everything lives in `C:\\dev\\Anchor` â€” plain markdown files are the source of truth (DASHBOARD.md, PROJECTS.md, INBOX.md, domain files), with no database, no syncing, and Python-stdlib-only code (one declared exception: optional `pywinpty` for terminals).\n\n- **What it ships as an app: `anchor_gui.py`, a self-contained local web server.** It generates the full dashboard HTML on every request, reads/writes the markdown directly, and runs persistently in the background as the NSSM Windows service `anchor` bound to `http://localhost:8777`. A CLI mirror (`anchor.py`) provides the same task operations and regenerates a static `dashboard.html`.\n\n- **Core task management.** Tasks move through a lifecycle â€” Active â†’ Done â†’ Cancelled / Saved-for-Later â†’ Restored â€” across the dashboard and per-domain files, all editable interactively in the browser, with every change logged.\n\n- **A layered R&D \"control surface\" built on top (v2 â†’ v3 â†’ v4).** This turns each project into a cockpit for \"trio\"-driven work (the researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman skills): per-lane sessions, cached/validated summaries, a Grass Catchers idea board, and pinnable deliverables.\n\n- **v3 \"Mission Control\" adds real interactive terminals.** ConPTY PTYs (`pty_manager.py`), per-session git-worktree isolation, a durable session registry, stage handoffs, an ephemeral deliverable-preview server (hard-guarded never to bind 8777), and Ghost World Labs branding.\n\n- **v4 \"Project Cockpit\" (built, merged to master, currently being deployed on this branch).** A Paradigm-2 layout of lane tiles with status lights and inline expanding panels (summary-over-terminal), a once-only skill auto-load/greet seed that fixes the repeating-prompt bug, a claudeâ†”gemini engine toggle, per-lane doc roles, a cost/tokens/time rollup, grass-promote-to-lane, and launch-by-type deliverables.\n\n- **Self-verifying.** A daily 5 AM health check (`anchor_healthcheck.py`) parses every file, boots a throwaway server, exercises every endpoint and the full v2/v3/v4 R&D surfaces fully stubbed (never the live `:8777` service, never live `claude`), and writes a dated report.\n\nNote: the current branch (`foreman/rnd-v4.1-cockpit`) has uncommitted work-in-progress on the v4.1 cockpit render (project window rendered as real Paradigm-2 tiles, per the latest commit and modified test files)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4410,"cache_read_input_tokens":45411,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4410,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a0f2b5c3-8b5e-4c2b-b62b-fdc42a390934","uuid":"24f81bf3-44a4-4038-9bc4-48368a6e0d82","request_id":"req_011Cc2Gub4HEGMhabSTSdNmd"}
